ofdrw/
  Source:  https://github.com/ofdrw/ofdrw
  Licence: Apache License 2.0
  Files:   test resources of the ofdrw modules, copied unmodified. The
           per-file origin paths are recorded in manifest.json.

gbt33190-samples/
  Source:  https://gitcode.com/open-source-toolkit/886653
           announced at
           https://blog.csdn.net/gitblog_09791/article/details/143283031
  Licence: published as conformance material alongside GB/T 33190-2016
           (Information technology - Open fixed-layout document). The sample
           set states no separate licence of its own; it is redistributed here
           for interoperability testing on the understanding that the samples
           exist to be parsed and validated.
  Files:   Desktop.zip as published, unmodified (11,616,209 bytes, sha256
           dcbd0e24cab4fdb251d149a7aeca711faeda513ababaea1d72080d35bcd1eb67).
           It contains ofd标准测试文件.zip, which contains the thirteen .ofd
           documents; both archives store their Chinese filenames as GBK.

gbt33190-standard/
  Source:  GB/T 33190-2016, Information technology - Open fixed-layout
           document (OFD), issued 2016-10-13, effective 2017-05-01. The
           record of the standard is
           https://openstd.samr.gov.cn/bzgk/std/newGbInfo?hcno=3AF6682D939116B6F5EED53D01A9DB5D
  Licence: none granted here. A Chinese national standard is not open
           licensed, and this repository claims no right over it. The PDF is
           the issued document, kept unmodified (5,068,468 bytes, sha256
           3c6da794cd5d2c33d968668583e5c0c909d1c0c554a2de37fb02788b72471051).
           The Markdown beside it is a transcription of the same document,
           made mechanically by SteleOFD and offered so that the standard can
           be read and searched; it is a derived reading, not the standard,
           and the PDF governs wherever the two differ. Both files are here
           for reference and interoperability work only. Neither is used as
           a test fixture by SteleOFD, whose own repository does not carry
           the standard's text.
           scripts/pdf_to_markdown.py is written for this repository and does
           nothing but turn the PDF above into the Markdown above; it is here
           rather than in SteleOFD for the same reason the text is.

